s.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "string", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a list of character codes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It evaluates the meaning of strings syntactically defined in the specific programming language, depending on the needs of the users.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "task", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that you have to do because it is part of your job", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need some help with that task now because this topic is very complex. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "syntactically", "type": "name"}, {"content": "related to the rules of syntax ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It evaluates the meaning of strings syntactically defined in the specific programming language, depending on the needs of the users.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "approach", "type": "name"}, {"content": "method", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  You have to study this topic more deeply to understand better. For example, there are four widely-used approaches to language semantics. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "linguistics", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the study of language", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In the past, we used the definition of semantics for linguistics only, nowadays, semantics is an important part of computer science.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Search for information about language semantics.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Identify the main idea and some other that complement it.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a mind-map to show what you understood about language semantics.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your mind-map in your class and discuss about the topic. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I search for information about language semantics. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify main and secondary ideas of language semantics. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a mind-map to show what I understood about language semantics.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share information about language semantics and discuss about it. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Simple Present and Simple Past with Time Expressions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span> to refer to routines, daily events, and things that usually happen or actions that you frequently do. </br>  You can use the <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span> tense to talk about actions that started and finished in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Simple Present</strong> </br> When you express general truths, you use <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span>. For example, the sentence \u201c<span class=\"italic\">Each country has a capital city</span>\u201d is a universal truth and it is stated in <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span>. </br></br>  Notice that for the subject pronouns <span class=\"strong\">I</span>, <span class=\"strong\">we</span>, <span class=\"strong\">you</span> and the <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span> form is equal to the infinitive, but for <span class=\"strong\">she</span>, <span class=\"strong\">he</span> or <span class=\"strong\">it</span> you need to include <span class=\"italic\">s/es</span> and you need the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">do/does</span> for the <span class =\"strong\">negative </span>and <span class =\"strong\">interrogative </span>form. There are some specific time expressions you can use for the <span class=\"strong\">simple present</span>, for example, <span class=\"strong\">every day</span>, <span class=\"strong\">today</span>, <span class=\"strong\">now</span>, <span class=\"strong\">this year</span>, <span class=\"strong\">nowadays</span>. </br></br>  Example</br> <span class=\"italic\">They design a new program <span class=\"strong\">this year</span>. </span></br>               <span class=\"italic\">They <span class =\"strong\">don't design </span>a new program. </span></br>              <span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\">Do </span>they <span class =\"strong\">design </span>a new program?</span> </br></br>                               <span class=\"italic\">The company designs software <span class=\"strong\">everyday</span>. </span></br>              <span class=\"italic\"> He doesn't design software <span class=\"strong\">at the moment</span>. </span></br>              <span class=\"italic\"><span class =\"strong\">Does Pedro </span>design software? </span>   </br></br>  <strong>Simple past </strong></br> You use the <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span> tense to talk about a complete event in the past. You can form the <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span> tense by adding <span class =\"strong\">ed</span>, <span class =\"strong\">-ied</span> to the verb when it is regular. For irregular verbs, you have to learn its particular change. There are some specific time expressions you can use for the <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span>, for example, <span class=\"strong\">yesterday</span>, <span class=\"strong\">last month</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">ago</span>. </br></br>  Example </br><span class=\"italic\">We designed a new program <span class=\"strong\">yesterday</span>. (regular verb) </br>                They studied in this institution <span class=\"strong\">last year</span>. (regular verb) </br>                He found new software 5 <span class=\"strong\">years ago</span>.</span> (irregular verb) </br></br>           You need auxiliary verb did for the <span class =\"strong\">negative  </span>and <span class =\"strong\">interrogative </span>form, for all the subject pronouns. </br></br>  Example</br> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class =\"strong\">didn't </span>design a new program.</span></br>         <span class=\"italic\">       <span class =\"strong\">Did </span>they study here?</span></br>         <span class=\"italic\">      He <span class =\"strong\">didn't </span>find the program. </span></br></br>  Notice that when you use the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">did</span>, the verb takes the infinitive form. </br></br>  Look at the chart of <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Present Simple</strong>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Questions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I/you/we/they\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I find a new program.  You send an email.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <strong>don't</strong> send new products.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><strong>Do</strong> they get products?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He/she/it\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He <strong>sells </strong>software</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <strong>doesn't</strong> buy software. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><strong>Does</strong> she buy a computer?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Simple Past</strong>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative  </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Questions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Regular verbs I/you/we/they/He/she/it\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class =\\\"strong\\\">watched </span>a new program. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We <strong>didn't</strong> send new products.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><strong>Did</strong> they get products?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Irregular verbs I/you/we/they/He/she/it\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He <span class =\\\"strong\\\">sold  </span>software</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <strong>didn't</strong> buy software. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><strong>Did</strong> she buy a computer?</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "What did you do yesterday?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wrote a report about language semantics but I didn't complete it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We know that semantics is the field concerned with mathematical structure and the meaning of programming languages.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Actions Verbs to Talk about Language Semantics", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Action verbs</span> are verbs that describe what the subject does.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">action verbs</span> show in a sentence what the subject is doing physically or mentally. </br></br>  It is important to consider that in English there are state verbs which are not commonly used in the <span class=\"strong\">present continuous</span> because they describe a state, not specifically an action. On the other hand, the verbs that you can use in the <span class=\"strong\">present simple</span> or <span class=\"strong\">continuous</span> are the action or dynamic verbs. </br></br>  Here some example of action verbs: <span class=\"strong\">define</span>, <span class=\"strong\">execute</span>, <span class=\"strong\">achieve</span>, <span class=\"strong\">write</span>, <span class=\"strong\">scale</span>, <span class=\"strong\">show</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">interpret</span>.", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}]}